cla_mmrs: describe the held CLA clock halt request

A clock halt action sets the global or local clock halt request, and the
request is held until the CLA reset; nothing in the register block clears
it. DisableGlobalClockHalt and DisableLocalClockHalt only block a new set,
and clearing EnableCla gates the CLA clock, which freezes the request. The
field descriptions read as a level that follows the action. This hold is the
intended behaviour, and the descriptions now say so.

Recorded as a patch so the hand-mirrored upstream/ tree stays
reproducible from the vendored spec plus patches/ applied in order.
diff --git a/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml b/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml
index c6a575f4c..78ac5a8a1 100644
--- a/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml
+++ b/rtl/mmr/spec/cla_mmrs.yml
@@ -3569,7 +3569,9 @@ c_dbg_cla_ctrl_status:
     FIELDS_RANGE: '15:15'
     RESET_VALUE: '0'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
-    DESCRIPTION: If this bit is set, clock halt action is not applied to local clocks
+    DESCRIPTION: If this bit is set, a clock halt action does not set the local
+      clock halt request. Setting it does not release a request already set; the
+      request is held until the CLA reset
     RESET_PORT: ''
     SW_WRITE: W
     SW_READ: R
@@ -3579,7 +3581,9 @@ c_dbg_cla_ctrl_status:
     FIELDS_RANGE: '14:14'
     RESET_VALUE: '0'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
-    DESCRIPTION: If this bit is set, clock halt action is not applied to global clocks
+    DESCRIPTION: If this bit is set, a clock halt action does not set the global
+      clock halt request. Setting it does not release a request already set; the
+      request is held until the CLA reset
     RESET_PORT: ''
     SW_WRITE: W
     SW_READ: R
@@ -3602,7 +3606,8 @@ c_dbg_cla_ctrl_status:
     DESCRIPTION: Set this bit to 1 to enable the CLA functional clock; clear it to 0
       to gate that clock (save pwr). The CLA register block runs on a clock whose
       functional enable is tied high, so this bit can still be written while the
-      functional clock is gated
+      functional clock is gated. Gating the clock freezes a held clock halt request
+      rather than releasing it
     MASKED_BY: ~cla_lock
     MASK_WRITES_ONLY?: 'True'
     RESET_PORT: ''
